  "userdoc": {
    "kind": "user",
    "methods": {
      "createDraftsModule(address)": {
        "notice": "Deploy a drafts proxy for `safe`. Permissionless on purpose: see         the contract docblock — a proxy is not an installation."
      },
      "createOwnerHistoryModule(address)": {
        "notice": "Deploy an owner-history proxy for `safe` and the guard bound to         it. Permissionless on purpose, same as `createDraftsModule`: the         guard is only live once the Safe calls `setGuard(guard)`, which         installs nothing but the guard slot."
      },
      "deployer()": {
        "notice": "The account that deployed the factory; the only address allowed         to move either implementation pointer."
      },
      "draftsImplementation()": {
        "notice": "The implementation the next `createDraftsModule` proxies onto."
      },
      "draftsModuleAddress(address)": {
        "notice": "The address the next `createDraftsModule(safe)` would deploy to,         for the current implementation and the current nonce. See the         three facts above."
      },
      "getDraftsImplementationByVersion(uint256)": {
        "notice": "1-based; reverts `InvalidVersion` outside `1..count`."
      },
      "getOwnerHistoryImplementationByVersion(uint256)": {
        "notice": "1-based; reverts `InvalidVersion` outside `1..count`."
      },
      "guardFor(address)": {
        "notice": "The guard deployed for `module`, or `address(0)` when this         factory deployed none. Answers zero rather than reverting: an         unknown module is a caller's mistake, not a reason a reader dies."
      },
      "ownerHistoryImplementation()": {
        "notice": "The implementation the next `createOwnerHistoryModule` proxies onto."
      },
      "ownerHistoryModuleAddress(address)": {
        "notice": "The address the next `createOwnerHistoryModule(safe)` would deploy         its proxy to. The guard is a plain CREATE with no predicted         address, and it is deployed after the proxy, so it cannot move         the proxy. See the three facts above."
      }
    },
    "notice": "The author side's one deploy path: a UUPS proxy per author Safe for         the drafts log, and a UUPS proxy per author Safe for the owner         history plus the `OwnerHistoryGuard` wired to that proxy.         One factory rather than two, because the two modules are installed         together on the same Safe and a reader that has this address has         every author proxy it can verify against. The two implementations         keep separate version histories — moving one must never silently         repoint the other. Trust model, stated because both halves are easy to get backwards:   - `setDraftsImplementation` / `setOwnerHistoryImplementation` are     `onlyDeployer`. Without that gate anyone could repoint the     `*Implementation()` pointer and the next `create*Module` would hand an     author a proxy that, once installed, executes as the Safe. The deployer     is an immutable set at construction, so there is no admin to rotate and     none to compromise.   - both `create*Module` stay open **deliberately**: deploying a proxy costs     the caller gas and installs nothing on any Safe. Nothing this contract     does reaches the Safe's storage — no `enableModule`, no `setGuard` — so a     proxy (and, for the history, a guard) is just two addresses until the     Safe adopts them in its own transaction. Gating creation would buy     nothing and would put a trusted party between an author and their own     module.   - `draftsModules` / `ownerHistoryModules` / `guards` are **indexes, not     proof**. `create*Module` is permissionless, so anyone can append an entry     for any Safe, and `guardFor` records what *this* factory made — it does     not prove the Safe installed it. Intersect the Safe's one real adoption     record (the guard slot) before treating an entry as installed.",
    "version": 1
  }
